 "text": "Hello, how are you doing? Not at all. It's better to be safe than sorry. For a wedding, a doctor's note is enough, is it? That's acceptable. Just carry it with you. And ask the bride to keep the food from the middle of the table. That's the toughest spot for vents in a church. No problem. Just ask the bride to keep the food off the middle of the table, and carry your note with you. Most brides are really understanding. You could say you' having it after so everyone can enjoy it without you being the center. Then you only need a small bit at the reception. You won't be. Brides appreciate your concern and will do their best to make you feel welcome.",
